        "evidence": "Claims verified. The relabelling map z -> 1/(1-z) and both stated identities check symbolically: 1/(1 - 1/(1-z)) = (z-1)/z = 1 - 1/z, and 1 - (1-z) = z, so the second edge parameter of the relabelled tetrahedron is the third of the original and the third is the first, exactly as the prose says. The Lean sibling QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_rotate resolves (IdealTriangulation.lean:206, namespace IdealTetrahedron) and states T.rotate.volume = T.volume, with rotate_shape giving 1/(1 - T.shape) and rotate_angles giving the 1->2->3->1 cycle."
